🧠 Product Thinking

Core hypothesis:
If teams can clearly see the financial and time cost of recurring meetings, they may be more likely to evaluate meeting duration, frequency, and attendance.

The product focuses on visibility rather than automatically labeling meetings as wasteful.

⚖️ Key Trade-offs

Accuracy vs Simplicity
The MVP uses employee compensation as the primary cost input rather than attempting to model every overhead cost.

Fun vs Professionalism
Relatable comparisons make the product memorable, while the core dashboard remains focused on business metrics.

Average Salary vs Individual Compensation
Quick calculation keeps onboarding simple, while advanced role-based inputs provide greater accuracy.

No Login vs Analytics
The MVP requires no account, reducing friction. Future versions could add saved meetings and team analytics.

